# RULES — IndustriaX Engineering Standards

> **Last Updated:** 2026-07-07
> **Format:** Industry-standard ID + Severity + Verifiable (modeled on OWASP, AWS Well-Architected, Google Engineering Practices)
> **Status:** Living document. Each rule has a Status field. Resolved rules move to the **Resolved Registry** at the bottom.
> **Companion:** [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md) for operating philosophy, communication style, and decision framework. [docs/ECONOMY_AUDIT.md](./docs/ECONOMY_AUDIT.md) for project status (Critical Focus section).
> **Audit basis:** Every rule was created because something broke, could break, or is currently broken. Rationale cites the originating incident.

---

## How to read this file

```
[DOMAIN-NNN]  Title
Severity: 🔴 Critical | 🟠 High | 🟡 Medium | 🟢 Low
Status:   Active | Resolved | Superseded
Statement: One imperative sentence.
Rationale: What incident / attack / regression created this rule.
Verify:    Lint command, test name, or manual checklist.
Example:   ❌ forbidden pattern  /  ✅ compliant pattern
```

**Rule IDs are stable.** When a rule is resolved, do not delete — move to the Resolved Registry with the resolution date and link to the fix.

**Active = enforceable now.** Critical and High rules must pass CI; Medium and Low rules are checked on review.

---

## SEC — Security

### [SEC-001] Server-authoritative game mutations
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Every economy-affecting game mutation MUST go through a server-side API endpoint with validation. Client-side mutations are forbidden for any value that affects player state.
- **Rationale:** Trading Post was originally 100% client-side Zustand mutations. Players cheated via browser console. Rebuilt as `/api/game/trade` in v15. **Must not regress.**
- **Verify:** Grep `setState` calls in `src/lib/game/actions/*.ts` for economy fields; each must be preceded by a successful server response. Architecture test in `tests/unit/tiers.test.ts` pattern.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN — client-only mutation
  set({ resources: { ...resources, iron: resources.iron - 100 } });

  // ✅ REQUIRED — server response drives state
  const result = await fetch('/api/game/trade', { ... });
  useGameStore.setState({ resources: result.resources });
  ```

### [SEC-002] Fail-closed on auth / lock / database errors
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** If authentication, account lock check, or database read fails, the operation MUST be **denied** (not allowed). Returning permissive defaults on error is a security hole.
- **Rationale:** Old `isAccountLocked` returned `{ locked: false }` on DB error → banned cheaters unlocked during Supabase outages. Old `verifyChecksum` had hardcoded fallback secret → anyone reading source could forge valid checksums.
- **Verify:** Every `catch` block in `src/lib/auth/*` and `src/lib/auth/gameStateValidator.ts` must return restrictive defaults. `isAccountLocked` must return `{ locked: true }` on all error paths (currently lines 502, 531).
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN — fail-open
  try { return { locked: false }; } catch { return { locked: false }; }

  // ✅ REQUIRED — fail-closed
  try { ... } catch (err) {
    console.error('[isAccountLocked] DB error', err);
    return { locked: true, reason: 'lock_check_unavailable' };
  }
  ```

### [SEC-003] No hardcoded secret fallbacks
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Required secrets (`CHECKSUM_SECRET`, Supabase service role key) MUST cause server boot to fail if missing. No fallback to hardcoded strings.
- **Rationale:** `process.env.CHECKSUM_SECRET || 'industriax-server-secret-2024'` would let any reader of source code forge valid anti-cheat checksums.
- **Verify:** `grep -r "process.env.X || " src/` should not return auth/secret lookups with hardcoded fallbacks. `gameStateValidator.ts:97-107` is the canonical example of the throw-on-missing pattern.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  const SECRET = process.env.CHECKSUM_SECRET || 'industriax-server-secret-2024';

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  const SECRET = process.env.CHECKSUM_SECRET;
  if (!SECRET) throw new Error('CHECKSUM_SECRET is required');
  ```

### [SEC-004] Pricing data must be finite or trade is rejected
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Server MUST reject any trade whose pricing-derived values (base/live/effective price, slippage, final amount) are non-finite. NaN / Infinity must never reach the client.
- **Rationale:** Bad Supabase row data (string in numeric column, null in required field) → `Number(...)` returns NaN → `JSON.stringify` serializes to `null` → client UI shows `null` silently. Better to 503 the trade.
- **Verify:** `src/app/api/game/trade/route.ts` must check `Number.isFinite(value)` for all 9 pricing fields before serializing the response.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN — silent NaN
  return NextResponse.json({ pricing: { giveBasePrice: Number(row.base_price), ... } });

  // ✅ REQUIRED — fail-closed
  if (!Number.isFinite(giveBasePrice) || !Number.isFinite(receiveSlippage) /* ... */) {
    console.error('[Trade] Pricing non-finite — rejecting');
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Pricing data unavailable', code: 'PRICING_INVALID' }, { status: 503 });
  }
  ```

### [SEC-005] No service role key on the client
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Supabase service role key MUST never appear in client-bundled code or be sent to the browser.
- **Rationale:** Service role bypasses RLS. If exposed, attacker can read/write any player data.
- **Verify:** `grep -r "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY" .next/static` should return zero matches after build. Only `src/lib/supabase/server.ts` may import it.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  // any file in src/components/ or src/app/ that's bundled to client
  import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js' with service role key;

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  // src/lib/supabase/server.ts (server-only, never imported by components)
  ```

### [SEC-006] No PII or production keys in committed files
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production` MUST be in `.gitignore` and MUST NOT be committed.
- **Rationale:** Production secrets in git history are unremovable without rewriting history.
- **Verify:** `cat .gitignore | grep -E "^\.env"` should show all env variants. Pre-commit hook (recommended) should refuse commits touching `.env*`.

### [SEC-007] Use `crypto.randomUUID()` for security-sensitive IDs
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** All security-sensitive IDs (session tokens, request IDs, audit IDs) MUST use `crypto.randomUUID()`. `Math.random()` is forbidden.
- **Rationale:** `Math.random()` is predictable and collision-prone.
- **Verify:** `grep -rn "Math.random" src/ tests/` — every occurrence should be for non-security purposes (visual jitter, etc.).
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  const id = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2);

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  const id = crypto.randomUUID();
  ```

### [SEC-008] Use `queueMicrotask()`, never `setImmediate()`, server-side
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Server-side async scheduling MUST use `queueMicrotask()` or `await`. `setImmediate()` is forbidden (does not exist in Edge runtime).
- **Rationale:** Edge runtime (Vercel, Cloudflare Workers) does not have `setImmediate`. Code that uses it crashes when deployed to edge.
- **Verify:** `grep -rn "setImmediate" src/` should return zero matches.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  setImmediate(() => logAction({ ... }));

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  queueMicrotask(() => logAction({ ... }));
  ```

### [SEC-009] Game speed must be validated against allowed set
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `gameSpeed` MUST be validated against `[1, 2, 5, 10]` both client-side and server-side. Any other value is rejected.
- **Rationale:** `setGameSpeed(1000)` → 1000 ticks/sec → browser crash, data corruption, unfair advantage.
- **Verify:** `src/lib/game/actions/core.ts:13-30` validates client-side. Server route `set_game_speed` action must re-validate.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  setGameSpeed: (speed: number) => set({ gameSpeed: speed })

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  const ALLOWED_SPEEDS = [1, 2, 5, 10] as const;
  setGameSpeed: (speed: number) => {
    if (!ALLOWED_SPEEDS.includes(speed as any)) return;
    set({ gameSpeed: speed });
  }
  ```

### [SEC-010] Caddyfile `XTransformPort` must be security-reviewed before changes
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Any change to the Caddyfile `XTransformPort` directive requires security review. It is an SSRF vector.
- **Rationale:** Unrestricted port forwarding enables attackers to reach internal services (Supabase, admin APIs, metadata endpoints).
- **Verify:** `grep "XTransformPort" Caddyfile` should match a known-good allowlist. PRs touching this directive require admin review.

---

## AUT — Authentication & Authorization

### [AUT-001] All API routes use `verifyAuth()` or `verifyAdmin()`
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Every API route that accesses player data MUST call `verifyAuth()` (or `verifyAdmin()` for admin routes) as the first line of the handler.
- **Rationale:** Unauthenticated routes leak data and allow unauthenticated mutations.
- **Verify:** `grep -L "verifyAuth\|verifyAdmin" src/app/api/**/route.ts` should return empty.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  export async function POST(request: Request) {
    const body = await request.json();
    // ... mutates state without auth check
  }

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  export async function POST(request: Request) {
    const auth = await verifyAuth();
    if (!auth.success) return auth.response;
    // ...
  }
  ```

### [AUT-002] Admin write operations require both `verifyAdmin()` and `canWrite()`
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Admin endpoints that mutate state MUST call BOTH `verifyAdmin()` and `canWrite()`. `verifyAdmin()` alone is insufficient.
- **Rationale:** The legacy `/api/admins` POST route only called `verifyAdmin()`, allowing viewer-role admins to escalate to super_admin.
- **Verify:** Every `src/app/api/admin/**/route.ts` POST/PUT/DELETE handler must contain `canWrite`.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN — verifyAdmin alone
  if (!verifyAdmin()) return ...;

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  const admin = await verifyAdmin();
  if (!admin.success) return admin.response;
  if (!canWrite(admin.role)) return forbidden();
  ```

### [AUT-003] Three-tier admin role model
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Admin roles MUST be one of `viewer`, `admin`, `super_admin`. No custom role names.
- **Rationale:** Custom roles bypass the `canWrite()` contract.
- **Verify:** `admin_users.role` is constrained by a CHECK or enum in the DB.
- **Roles:**
  - `viewer` — read-only
  - `admin` — read + write all admin data
  - `super_admin` — admin role management + all admin capabilities

### [AUT-004] Guest accounts gated from premium features
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Guest accounts MUST be blocked from `/api/game/trade`, market place, leaderboard, and mega-projects. They MUST be prompted to link an account to access these.
- **Rationale:** Guest mode is for trial / casual play. Economy-affecting features require real identity to prevent ban evasion.
- **Verify:** `getUserGuestStatus()` check in premium routes. `LoginFloatingPanel` shows for guests in `useTabChange`.

---

## API — API Contract & Rate Limiting

### [API-001] Every API route has rate limiting
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Every API route that performs mutations or expensive reads MUST use `checkRateLimit()`. Public read endpoints (definitions, market state) MUST have a low rate limit.
- **Rationale:** Unrate-limited endpoints enable brute-force attacks, scraping, and DoS.
- **Verify:** `grep -L "checkRateLimit" src/app/api/**/route.ts` should be empty.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ✅ REQUIRED
  const rateLimitResponse = await checkRateLimit(auth.userId, RATE_LIMITS.action, '/api/game/trade');
  if (rateLimitResponse) return rateLimitResponse;
  ```

### [API-002] Rate limit profile per route purpose
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Each API route MUST use an appropriate rate limit profile from `RATE_LIMITS` in `src/lib/auth/rateLimiter.ts`. Anti-abuse for critical endpoints, generous for read endpoints.
- **Rationale:** One-size-fits-all rate limiting either blocks legitimate users or fails to stop abuse.
- **Verify:** `RATE_LIMITS` enum in `rateLimiter.ts` defines named profiles (action, read, auth, market). Every route uses a named profile.

### [API-003] Server returns fail-closed on rate limit failure
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** If the rate limiter errors, the request MUST be **denied** with 429, not allowed.
- **Rationale:** Same fail-closed principle as [SEC-002]. Rate limiter downtime shouldn't open a hole.

### [API-004] API routes return consistent error format
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Error responses MUST use `{ error: string, code?: string }`. Success responses include relevant data.
- **Rationale:** Predictable shape makes client error handling and admin debugging consistent.
- **Verify:** `grep -E "NextResponse.json.+\berror\b" src/app/api/**/route.ts` should match `error` field consistently.

### [API-005] Routes grouped by domain
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Game routes go under `/api/game/`, admin under `/api/admin/`, config under `/api/config/`, auth under `/api/auth/`, market under `/api/market/`, leaderboard under `/api/leaderboard/`, cron under `/api/cron/`, health under `/api/health/`.
- **Rationale:** Domain grouping makes the 64-route surface scannable.

### [API-006] `validActions` and `actionType` union must stay in sync
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Adding a new action type requires updating BOTH the `validActions` array AND the handler switch. Dead entries are forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Dead entries in `validActions` waste server time and mask missing implementations. Reject via validation rather than silently hit `default: 'Unhandled action'`.
- **Verify:** Current `validActions` in `src/app/api/game/action/route.ts:413-423` has 7 actions: `build`, `sell`, `buy`, `research`, `upgrade`, `transport`, `set_game_speed`. Any new action must be added in lockstep.

---

## DB — Database & Data Integrity

### [DB-001] All schema changes via Supabase SQL migrations
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Schema changes MUST be in `supabase/migrations/<timestamp>_<seq>_<description>.sql`. Application code MUST NOT issue DDL.
- **Rationale:** Migrations are the source of truth and roll-forward mechanism. Schema in code is invisible to ops.
- **Verify:** Every table present in production has a migration file. `ls supabase/migrations/ | wc -l` is the migration count (currently 81).

### [DB-002] Every new table has RLS enabled
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Every new table MUST include `ALTER TABLE xxx ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;` plus policies for read/write. Service-role bypass policies are required for server-side operations.
- **Rationale:** Defense-in-depth. Even if app code has a bug, RLS prevents data leaks.
- **Verify:** `grep -L "ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY" supabase/migrations/*.sql` for any new tables created.

### [DB-003] Standard RLS policy set
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** New user-data tables MUST have:
  - `SELECT` policy: `USING (user_id = auth.uid())`
  - `INSERT` policy: `WITH CHECK (user_id = auth.uid())`
  - `UPDATE` policy: `USING (user_id = auth.uid())` and `WITH CHECK (user_id = auth.uid())`
  - `DELETE` policy (if applicable): `USING (user_id = auth.uid())`
  - Service-role bypass: `TO service_role USING (true) WITH CHECK (true)`
- **Rationale:** Consistent policy structure makes audit easier.

### [DB-004] Use `TIMESTAMPTZ` for all timestamps
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** All timestamp columns MUST use `TIMESTAMPTZ`. `TIMESTAMP` (without timezone) is forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Server and client timezones differ. `TIMESTAMPTZ` normalizes to UTC.
- **Verify:** `grep -E "TIMESTAMP[^Z]" supabase/migrations/*.sql` should return zero.

### [DB-005] Use INTEGER (cents) or DECIMAL for money
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Monetary values MUST use `INTEGER` (cents) or `DECIMAL`. `FLOAT` / `REAL` / `DOUBLE PRECISION` is forbidden for money.
- **Rationale:** Floating-point arithmetic causes rounding errors that compound over time.
- **Verify:** `grep -E "money.*FLOAT|money.*REAL" supabase/` should return zero.

### [DB-006] CHECK constraints on bounded numeric fields
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Fields with natural bounds (money >= 0, level 1-100, cheat flag count 0-3) MUST have `CHECK` constraints in the DB as the last line of defense.
- **Rationale:** App-level validation can be bypassed. DB constraints cannot.
- **Verify:** `player_progress.money` has `CHECK (money >= 0)`. New bounded fields should follow the same pattern.
- **Example:**
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE game_state (
    money BIGINT NOT NULL CHECK (money >= 0),
    level INTEGER NOT NULL CHECK (level BETWEEN 1 AND 100)
  );
  ```

### [DB-007] SQL atomic increments for read-modify-write
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Concurrent counter mutations (cheat flags, balances, vote counts) MUST use SQL atomic operations (`UPDATE ... SET col = col + 1` or RPCs), not read-then-write.
- **Rationale:** Read-then-write has a TOCTOU race that loses increments under concurrent requests.
- **Verify:** `increment_cheat_flag` RPC in `src/lib/db/cheatInvestigations.ts:300-319` is the canonical pattern.
- **Example:**
  ```sql
  -- ❌ FORBIDDEN — read then write
  SELECT cheat_flag_count INTO x FROM profiles WHERE ...;
  UPDATE profiles SET cheat_flag_count = x + 1 WHERE ...;

  -- ✅ REQUIRED — atomic in single statement
  UPDATE profiles SET cheat_flag_count = cheat_flag_count + 1 WHERE id = ...;
  ```

### [DB-008] Indexes on `user_id` and `created_at`
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Every table MUST have indexes on `user_id` (for RLS performance) and `created_at` (for time-range queries). Composite indexes SHOULD be added for common query patterns.
- **Rationale:** Without indexes, RLS-scoped queries do full table scans, killing performance at scale.

### [DB-009] Idempotent migrations where possible
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Migrations SHOULD use `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`, `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS`, etc., where the SQL dialect supports it.
- **Rationale:** Idempotent migrations can be safely re-run during recovery or partial failures.

### [DB-010] One logical change per migration file
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Each migration file MUST contain a single logical change. Do not combine unrelated changes.
- **Rationale:** Easier to review, easier to revert if needed.
- **Verify:** Filename format `<timestamp>_<seq>_<description>.sql` (e.g., `20260707120000_068_tier5_full_wiring.sql`).

### [DB-011] No raw SQL outside migration files
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Application code MUST NOT execute raw DDL. Schema lives in migrations only.
- **Rationale:** Untracked schema is invisible to ops and breaks rollbacks.

### [DB-012] Prisma is forbidden
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Prisma MUST NOT be used. The Prisma directory was removed; do not reintroduce.
- **Rationale:** The original `prisma/schema.prisma` was the Next.js starter's SQLite User/Post model — running `prisma db:push` would have created wrong tables in Supabase PostgreSQL.

---

## STO — State Management (Zustand)

### [STO-001] Use specific Zustand selectors
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Components MUST subscribe via `useGameStore((s) => s.specificField)`. `useGameStore()` without a selector is forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Full-store subscription causes re-renders on every tick (~10-100/sec). Mobile users experience severe lag.
- **Verify:** `grep -rn "useGameStore()" src/components/` should return zero matches. `grep -rn "useGameStore()" src/lib/hooks/` is allowed only if followed by a selector.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  const store = useGameStore();
  const money = store.money;

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  const money = useGameStore((s) => s.money);
  const resources = useGameStore((s) => s.resources);
  ```

### [STO-002] Single source of truth for game state
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `useGameStore` is the ONLY Zustand store for game data. New game-state stores are forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Multiple stores fragment state, require cross-store coordination, and break server-cloud sync.
- **Verify:** `grep -rn "create<" src/lib/game/` — only `useGameStore` should be a game-state store. `useSettingsStore` is allowed for UI preferences.

### [STO-003] Store actions are the only mutation path
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Components MUST NOT call `useGameStore.setState()` directly for game data. They MUST invoke a store action.
- **Rationale:** Direct setState bypasses validation, audit logging, and side effects (debounced persist, market pressure).
- **Verify:** `grep -rn "useGameStore.setState" src/components/` should return zero matches for game fields. Only server responses may call setState (to apply authoritative state).

### [STO-004] Save version incremented on state shape change
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** When adding new state fields, `SAVE_VERSION` MUST be incremented and a migration entry added to `migrateSaveState()`.
- **Rationale:** Past migrations V1→V19 show that adding state fields without version increments causes player data loss.

### [STO-005] Debounced persistence (5s) and cloud sync (2 min)
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Local persistence uses 5s debounce. Cloud save to `/api/game/state` runs every 2 minutes. Do NOT increase frequency.
- **Rationale:** More frequent saves overload the server. Less frequent risks more data loss.
- **Verify:** `debouncedPersistStorage` debounce window is 5000ms. `CloudSyncService.startAutoSave` interval is 60000ms.

### [STO-006] `beforeunload` flush listener MUST stay
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** The `beforeunload` event listener that flushes pending writes MUST NOT be removed.
- **Rationale:** Page close is the most common data-loss moment. **Known limitation:** on mobile force-kill, `beforeunload` may not fire. This is acceptable; periodic saves (every 2 min) limit the loss window.

### [STO-007] Single state version source
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** The store version is incremented on every successful server-side write. Client increments MUST be optimistic and verified by the server response.
- **Rationale:** Optimistic locking on `state_version` field prevents concurrent write conflicts (e.g., two parallel trades overwriting each other).

---

## UI — UI / Frontend

### [UI-001] Game panels go in `src/components/game/`
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Game panels MUST live in `src/components/game/`. Shared subcomponents in `src/components/game/shared/`. UI primitives in `src/components/ui/` (shadcn).
- **Rationale:** Predictable structure makes component discovery and architecture tests work.
- **Verify:** Currently 55 game panels in `src/components/game/`.

### [UI-002] Never modify shadcn/ui primitives directly
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Components in `src/components/ui/` are managed by the shadcn CLI. Direct modifications will be overwritten on update.
- **Rationale:** shadcn-ui rewrites files on CLI re-runs. Changes should be in custom wrappers, not primitives.
- **Verify:** `git log --follow src/components/ui/button.tsx` should show no manual edits.

### [UI-003] Use shadcn primitives + `cn()` for class composition
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Custom components MUST use shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Select`, etc.) and the `cn()` utility for conditional classes.
- **Rationale:** Consistency and Tailwind class deduplication.

### [UI-004] `GameIcon` for all game icons
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Game icons MUST go through `<GameIcon icon={...} />`. Raw emoji or Lucide inline icons in game panels are forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Centralized icon registry with tier/category theming.

### [UI-005] Tier centralization SSOT
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Tier metadata (colors, info) MUST come from `src/lib/game/tiers.ts` (`TIER_INFO`, `MAX_TIER`, `ALL_TIERS`). Hardcoded tier arrays like `[0, 1, 2, 3]` are forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Pre-Phase-5.5, 6 panel files had duplicated tier systems. Architecture test enforces the SSOT.
- **Verify:** `tests/unit/tiers.test.ts` scans all panels for hardcoded tier arrays. Must always pass.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN
  const TIER_COLORS = ['#a0a0a0', '#22d3ee', '#fbbf24'];

  // ✅ REQUIRED
  import { TIER_INFO, getTierColor } from '@/lib/game/tiers';
  const color = getTierColor(2);
  ```

### [UI-006] Responsive breakpoints
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Game panels MUST be responsive: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints. Mobile-first approach for trade post, market, dashboard.
- **Rationale:** 60%+ of players use mobile.
- **Verify:** Manual mobile test (DevTools responsive mode) for every new panel.

### [UI-007] AnimatePresence for dynamic lists
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Lists that change frequently (notifications, history) MUST use Framer Motion's `AnimatePresence` for entry/exit animations.
- **Rationale:** Smooth visual transitions for list mutations.

### [UI-008] Long lists must scroll, not overflow
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Lists longer than 6 items MUST have `max-h-64 overflow-y-auto game-scrollbar`.
- **Rationale:** Prevents layout shift and frame drops on long content.

---

## PER — Performance

### [PER-001] All queries use indexed columns in WHERE
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Database queries MUST use indexed columns in `WHERE` clauses. RLS policies implicitly filter by `user_id`, which is indexed.
- **Rationale:** Unindexed queries do full table scans. At 10K+ players, this kills performance.
- **Verify:** `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` for any new query path.

### [PER-002] All list endpoints have LIMIT
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** List-returning endpoints MUST cap results with `LIMIT`. Default 50, max 200.
- **Rationale:** Unbounded list responses can be megabytes. DoS surface.

### [PER-003] Avoid `SELECT *`, specify columns
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Queries MUST specify columns: `select('id, name, created_at')`. `select('*')` is forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Avoids over-fetching. Makes the data shape explicit.

### [PER-004] N+1 queries are forbidden
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** API routes MUST NOT issue N+1 queries. Use JOINs, batch selects, or RPCs.
- **Rationale:** 100 players × 5 building types = 500 round-trips. O(n²) latency.

### [PER-005] Cache game config server-side
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Game config (buildings, resources, market) is cached in memory via `configCache` + `balanceConfig` + `configLoader.server`. Reload on changes via 60s poller + `instrumentation.ts` pre-warm at boot.
- **Rationale:** Config rarely changes. Re-fetching on every request adds 50-300ms latency.
- **Verify:** `src/lib/game/configLoader.server.ts` (60s poller) + `instrumentation.ts` (pre-warm).

### [PER-006] Use `createServiceRoleClient()` only when RLS bypass is required
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Server-side code MUST use the regular client unless it specifically needs to bypass RLS (admin operations, cross-user data).
- **Rationale:** Service role bypasses all RLS — even your own policies. Audit cost.

### [PER-007] Presence channel refresh >= 10s
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Supabase Presence refresh interval MUST be 10s or higher. Currently 30s.
- **Rationale:** Faster refresh overloads the realtime channel. 30s is sufficient for "is player online" UX.

### [PER-008] No background polling loops
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Components MUST NOT start their own `setInterval` polling loops. Use the existing hooks (`useServerMarket`, `useOnlinePresence`) which centralize polling.
- **Rationale:** 50 components each with their own poll = 50 concurrent requests to Supabase. Single shared hook = 1 request.

### [PER-009] Server-authoritative state minimization
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Client-server state synchronization MUST minimize payload. Only sync the fields that changed.
- **Rationale:** Trade post returns the full `updatedState.resources` rather than a diff. For 14 resources this is small; for a real game with 80+ it matters.

### [PER-010] API responses < 200ms p95
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** API routes MUST return within 200ms at p95. Routes that violate this need caching or refactor.
- **Rationale:** User-perceived latency. 200ms is the perception threshold.

---

## ARC — Architecture

### [ARC-001] Client authoritative for gameplay, server authoritative for validation
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** The game loop runs client-side for responsiveness. The server validates, persists, and detects cheats. **This is a documented tradeoff** — server-side state and client-side state may briefly diverge.
- **Rationale:** Server-authoritative tick loops add 50-200ms latency per tick, making the game feel sluggish. Idle games accept eventual consistency.
- **Verify:** `instrumentation.ts` log "Game config pre-warmed successfully" at boot. Cloud sync runs every 2 min.

### [ARC-002] Game config is server-controlled, not bundled
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** All game-tuning values (buildings, recipes, balance constants, prices) MUST come from Supabase at runtime. Hardcoded client-side values for these are forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Operators need to tune the game without redeploying. Client-bundled values can't be changed without a release.
- **Verify:** `data.ts` is empty/removed. `configCache.ts` and `balanceConfig.ts` are the SSOTs. `tiers.ts` defines tier constants.
- **Example:**
  ```ts
  // ❌ FORBIDDEN — bundled game data
  const BUILDING_DEFS = { ironMine: { baseCost: [{ resource: 'money', amount: 400 }] } };

  // ✅ REQUIRED — fetched from Supabase
  const config = await ensureConfigLoaded();
  const def = config.buildings.ironMine;
  ```

### [ARC-003] Server config cache with TTL
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Game config MUST be cached in `configCache` and refreshed via TTL (60s for balance) or explicit invalidation. Components MUST read from the cache, not re-fetch.
- **Rationale:** 50 components each fetching config = 50 requests per config change. Centralized cache = 1.

### [ARC-004] `configCache` SSOT pattern
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `src/lib/game/configCache.ts` and `src/lib/game/balanceConfig.ts` are the SSOTs for game config. `src/lib/game/tiers.ts` is the SSOT for tier metadata. `src/lib/game/configLoader.server.ts` is the SSOT for server config loading.
- **Rationale:** Multiple SSOTs, each for a different concern. The "Code Reference" appendix lists them.

### [ARC-005] Feature-based modular architecture
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Code is organized by business domain, not by file type. Each feature owns its components, store, types, services, data, hooks.
- **Rationale:** Easier to navigate, easier to decompose.
- **Verify:** 21 action files in `src/lib/game/actions/` are feature-grouped (buildings, contracts, drones, market, etc.).

### [ARC-006] File size limits
- **Severity:** 🟢 Low
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Ideal: 300-500 LOC. Acceptable: 800-1200. Hard limit: 2000. Files exceeding limits MUST be decomposed.
- **Rationale:** Past `store.ts` was 3,637 lines; after Phase 5.5, it's 148 lines (barrel) with 21 action files.

### [ARC-007] Decompose legacy monolithic files
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Files that grew >1000 LOC MUST be decomposed into feature-specific files. Decomposition pattern: barrel `index.ts` + feature files.
- **Rationale:** Single-file god classes are unmaintainable.

### [ARC-008] Game-action handler array stays in sync
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `validActions` array and `actionType` union must be updated together. The handler switch in `/api/game/action` must implement every name in `validActions`.
- **Rationale:** Dead entries waste server time and mask missing implementations.

### [ARC-009] No game logic in React components
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Business logic (calculations, mutations, side effects) MUST live in the Zustand store or server-side. React components are for rendering and user input only.
- **Rationale:** Logic in components is hard to test, hard to share, and runs on every render.
- **Verify:** Components should not import calculation utilities. They invoke store actions.

### [ARC-010] `tiers.ts` is the tier metadata SSOT
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** All tier metadata (TIER_INFO, MAX_TIER, ALL_TIERS, getTierColor, getTierInfo, isValidTier) lives in `src/lib/game/tiers.ts`. `src/lib/game/icons/tiers.ts` is a backward-compat redirect.
- **Rationale:** Pre-Phase-5.5 had 6 duplicated tier systems. Architecture test enforces.
- **Verify:** `tests/unit/tiers.test.ts` scans all panels for hardcoded tier arrays. Must pass.

---

## PRF — Production / Deployment

### [PRF-001] No secrets in code or committed files
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Production secrets MUST NOT appear in code, comments, or committed files. `.env*` files are gitignored.
- **Rationale:** See [SEC-006].

### [PRF-002] Lint passes on `src/`
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `npm run lint` (or `bun run lint`) MUST pass with 0 errors before any commit.
- **Verify:** `npm run lint` exits 0.

### [PRF-003] TypeScript clean
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `bunx tsc --noEmit` MUST pass with 0 errors.
- **Verify:** `bunx tsc --noEmit` exits 0.

### [PRF-004] All vitest tests pass
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** `npm run test:vitest` MUST pass. Currently 65/65 tests across 14 files.
- **Rationale:** Test suite includes API tests, JWT verification, balance config validators, tier centralization architecture tests, and game tick input-floor tests.
- **Verify:** `bunx vitest run` returns 65 passed.

### [PRF-005] Architecture tests enforced
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** The architecture test in `tests/unit/tiers.test.ts` MUST pass. It scans all panels for hardcoded tier arrays and fails the build if any are found.
- **Rationale:** Catches SSOT violations automatically.

### [PRF-006] No regression to client-only mutations
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Trading Post, market, contracts, prestige, drones, workers, automation, and all economy-affecting features MUST go through server-side APIs. Client-only mutations are forbidden.
- **Rationale:** Client-only mutations allow cheating via browser console. C5 was a critical security incident.

### [PRF-007] Pre-deploy smoke test on critical pages
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Before any production deploy, manually load `/`, `/game/dashboard`, `/game/tradePost`, `/game/market`, `/admin/` and verify they render without console errors.
- **Rationale:** Catches SSR errors, hydration mismatches, and missing dependencies that lint/tests don't.

### [PRF-008] Migration files included in commit
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Any new `supabase/migrations/*.sql` file MUST be in the same commit that depends on it. Migrations MUST be applied to production before the corresponding code deploy.
- **Rationale:** Migrations out of sync with code = broken app.

### [PRF-009] `CHECKSUM_SECRET` set in production
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** Production environment MUST have `CHECKSUM_SECRET` set. Server fails to boot if missing (see [SEC-003]).
- **Verify:** Vercel env var present. Boot log shows "Game config pre-warmed successfully".

### [PRF-010] Update `docs/ECONOMY_AUDIT.md` on phase completion
- **Severity:** 🟡 Medium
- **Status:** Active
- **Statement:** When a phase (tier wiring, balance config migration, market audit) is complete, update `docs/ECONOMY_AUDIT.md` with the new status. The "Critical Focus" section at the top must always be current.
- **Rationale:** Single source of truth for project state.

