## Industry Standards Applicability

> **Context:** IndustriaX is a browser-based idle game (Next.js 16 + Supabase + Zustand), single-player-per-account with shared global market simulation. No PII commerce, no enterprise customers yet, no SLA contracts. Standards below are tagged:
> - **Apply** — already enforced via rules above or actively used
> - **Partial** — partially in place; gap documented
> - **Future** — relevant but not yet implemented (planning post-launch)
> - **N/A** — not applicable to this product/scale

### A11y / Accessibility

### [STD-A11y-001] WCAG 2.1 AA compliance
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All UI components MUST meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA at minimum.
- **Rationale:** Browser app, public users, includes color-blind players. Accessibility is not optional.
- **Verify:** `<input>` elements have associated `<label>`, buttons have `aria-label` for icon-only, contrast ratio ≥ 4.5:1 for normal text. Use axe DevTools in browser.

### [STD-A11y-002] Keyboard navigation
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All game actions MUST be reachable via keyboard.
- **Rationale:** Many game panels are dense; keyboard shortcuts are essential for power users.
- **Verify:** Existing `useKeyboardShortcuts` hook in `src/lib/hooks/page/`. Document all shortcuts in `/guide` page.

### UX / UI / DX

### [STD-UX-001] Mobile-first responsive design
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All game panels MUST be designed mobile-first with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints.
- **Rationale:** 80%+ of players use mobile. [UI-006].
- **Verify:** Manual test in DevTools responsive mode for every new panel.

### [STD-UX-002] Design system via shadcn/ui
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All UI components MUST use shadcn/ui primitives (`Button`, `Card`, `Select`, etc.) — no custom HTML button/card implementations.
- **Rationale:** [UI-002] + [UI-003]. Consistency, accessibility baked in.
- **Verify:** `src/components/ui/` only modified by shadcn CLI, not by hand.

### [STD-UX-003] Atomic component decomposition
- **Applicability:** Partial
- **Statement:** Game panels SHOULD be decomposed into atoms (icon, badge), molecules (resource row), organisms (panel).
- **Rationale:** Atomic Design — currently 55 panels, some are monolithic. Decompose opportunistically.
- **Verify:** No hard rule; opportunistic during refactors.

### [STD-UX-004] Dark mode support
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** The game MUST support dark mode (current default).
- **Rationale:** shadcn/ui ships dark mode variants; theme is consistent.
- **Verify:** `dark:` classes used in panels. Light theme not required.

### [STD-UX-005] No emoji in production UI
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Game icons MUST go through `<GameIcon />`. Emoji in production UI is forbidden.
- **Rationale:** [UI-004]. Emoji renders inconsistently across platforms.
- **Verify:** `grep -r "[ð-÷]" src/components/` should not find emoji literals.

### [STD-UX-006] Developer experience — fast feedback loops
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** TypeScript + Vitest + ESLint + Biome MUST run in <30s on dev machine.
- **Rationale:** DX — slow tools kill productivity.
- **Verify:** `npm run test:vitest` < 30s, `npm run lint` < 15s, `bunx tsc --noEmit` < 30s.

### [STD-API-001] REST-style HTTP API
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All endpoints MUST follow REST conventions (resource-oriented paths, proper HTTP verbs).
- **Rationale:** REST is the standard for our 64 endpoints; no need for GraphQL.
- **Verify:** See [API-005] — routes grouped by domain under `/api/<domain>/`.

### [STD-API-002] OpenAPI specification (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** All endpoints SHOULD have an OpenAPI 3.1 spec for client SDK generation.
- **Rationale:** Would help external integrators (mods, analytics dashboards). Not yet a need.
- **Verify:** Generate from Zod schemas + route handlers (e.g., `zod-to-openapi`). Defer until external API consumers exist.

### [STD-API-003] API-first design
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Backend API contract MUST be designed BEFORE frontend implementation.
- **Rationale:** Server-authoritative architecture ([SEC-001]) requires API to be the source of truth.
- **Verify:** Feature dev workflow in AGENTS.md — design API layer (step 5b) before store actions (step 6) and UI (step 7).

### [STD-API-004] Webhooks (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Outbound webhooks SHOULD be supported for player events (trade completion, contract fulfillment).
- **Rationale:** Would enable third-party integrations (Discord bots, analytics).
- **Verify:** No current use case. Defer until needed.

### [STD-AUTH-001] OAuth 2.0 / OIDC via Supabase Auth
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Authentication MUST go through Supabase Auth (which uses OAuth 2.0 / OIDC under the hood).
- **Rationale:** Supabase Auth is the standard for this stack. We don't run our own auth.
- **Verify:** No custom auth code outside `src/lib/auth/orchestrator/` + Supabase client.

### [STD-AUTH-002] JWT for session tokens
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Session tokens MUST be JWT (issued by Supabase).
- **Rationale:** Standard. Trust boundary is JWT verification on each server-side handler.
- **Verify:** `verifyAuth()` decodes JWT and fetches user. See [AUT-001].

### [STD-AUTH-003] RBAC for admin operations
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Admin authorization MUST use Role-Based Access Control (viewer / admin / super_admin).
- **Rationale:** [AUT-002], [AUT-003]. Standard 3-tier model.
- **Verify:** `canWrite()` checks role before mutation.

### [STD-AUTH-004] ABAC (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Attribute-based access control MAY be added for fine-grained rules (e.g., admin can only manage players in their region).
- **Rationale:** Not needed at current scale.
- **Verify:** N/A until multi-tenant or region-based access becomes a requirement.

### [STD-AUTH-005] SSO / MFA / 2FA (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** SSO and MFA MAY be supported via Supabase Auth's enterprise features.
- **Rationale:** Single-player game, no enterprise customers yet. Supabase Auth supports it natively if/when needed.
- **Verify:** N/A until enterprise sales require it.

### [STD-SEC-001] OWASP Top 10 mitigation
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Project MUST mitigate OWASP Top 10 (2021): broken access control, crypto failures, injection, insecure design, misconfiguration, vulnerable components, auth failures, data integrity, logging failures, SSRF.
- **Rationale:** All SEC-* rules in this document are derived from OWASP. See SEC-001 to SEC-010.
- **Verify:** Each SEC-* rule maps to one or more OWASP categories.

### [STD-SEC-002] CSP via Vercel headers
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Production MUST set a Content-Security-Policy header (allowlist scripts/styles).
- **Rationale:** Defense-in-depth against XSS.
- **Verify:** `next.config.ts` or `vercel.json` sets CSP header. Test via browser DevTools → Response Headers.

### [STD-SEC-003] CSRF protection
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All state-changing endpoints MUST be protected against CSRF (SameSite cookies + Origin check).
- **Rationale:** Supabase Auth cookies are SameSite=Lax by default. Origin check on mutating routes is additional defense.
- **Verify:** POST endpoints verify `request.headers.get('origin')` matches expected origin.

### [STD-SEC-004] CORS policy
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** API endpoints MUST have a defined CORS policy (allowlist specific origins).
- **Rationale:** Prevent unauthorized browser origins from calling API.
- **Verify:** Next.js `next.config.ts` `headers()` defines CORS. Default same-origin.

### [STD-SEC-005] Rate limiting per route
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Every API route MUST have rate limiting. See [API-001], [API-002].
- **Rationale:** Standard DoS protection.
- **Verify:** `grep -L "checkRateLimit" src/app/api/**/route.ts` returns empty.

### [STD-SEC-006] Audit logs for all mutations
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All player mutations and admin mutations MUST be logged to `player_actions` / `admin_actions` tables.
- **Rationale:** Standard for forensics + cheat detection.
- **Verify:** `logActionAsync()` called from all mutating routes.

### [STD-SEC-007] GDPR / CCPA (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** When launching in EU/CA jurisdictions, MUST implement data subject rights (export, delete).
- **Rationale:** Not yet applicable; Supabase supports row-level deletion if/when needed.
- **Verify:** N/A until launch in regulated jurisdictions.

### [STD-SEC-008] SOC 2 / ISO 27001 (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Certification is not currently pursued.
- **Rationale:** Pre-revenue / no enterprise customers.
- **Verify:** N/A.

### [STD-SEC-009] Encryption at rest
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All data at rest MUST be encrypted by storage layer.
- **Rationale:** Supabase PostgreSQL uses encrypted disks. Not configurable from app code.
- **Verify:** Supabase project settings confirm encryption enabled.

### [STD-SEC-010] Encryption in transit
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** All network traffic MUST use HTTPS/TLS.
- **Rationale:** Vercel enforces HTTPS by default. Caddy terminates TLS.
- **Verify:** `curl -I https://industryx.vercel.app` returns `HTTP/2 200` with valid cert.

### Observability

### [STD-OBS-001] Structured logging
- **Applicability:** Partial
- **Statement:** All server-side logs SHOULD be structured (`[Component] message`, key=value) for parsing.
- **Rationale:** Easier debugging in Vercel logs.
- **Verify:** `grep -r "console.log" src/` should mostly return structured `[Component] message` patterns.

### [STD-OBS-002] Metrics collection (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Production SHOULD emit metrics (request duration, error rate, queue depth) to a metrics backend.
- **Rationale:** Vercel provides basic analytics; deeper metrics (PostHog, Datadog) deferred.
- **Verify:** N/A — defer until traffic warrants.

### [STD-OBS-003] Distributed tracing (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Cross-service request tracing MAY be added when service count grows.
- **Rationale:** Single Next.js app currently; no service-to-service tracing needed yet.
- **Verify:** N/A.

### [STD-OBS-004] Health check endpoint
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** `/api/health` MUST return 200 when Supabase is reachable.
- **Rationale:** Standard for uptime monitoring.
- **Verify:** `curl https://industryx.vercel.app/api/health` returns 200.

### [STD-OBS-005] SLO / SLA / SLI
- **Applicability:** N/A
- **Statement:** No external SLA contracts yet.
- **Rationale:** Pre-revenue. Once paid users exist, define p99 latency, error rate, uptime targets.
- **Verify:** N/A until paid launch.

### CI/CD & DevOps

### [STD-CI-001] CI pipeline runs lint + typecheck + tests
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Every PR MUST pass `npm run lint`, `bunx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run test:vitest` before merge.
- **Rationale:** Standard CI hygiene.
- **Verify:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (or Vercel build pipeline) runs all three.

### [STD-CI-002] Trunk-based development
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Branches MUST be short-lived (<3 days). Main branch is always deployable.
- **Rationale:** Modern standard over GitFlow.
- **Verify:** No long-running feature branches. Force-push discouraged.

### [STD-CI-003] Semantic versioning (SemVer)
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Release tags MUST follow MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH.
- **Rationale:** Standard.
- **Verify:** `git tag --list` shows vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH pattern.

### [STD-CI-004] Conventional Commits
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Commit messages MUST follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, etc.).
- **Rationale:** Standard. Enables auto-changelog generation.
- **Verify:** `.agents/skills/caveman-commit/SKILL.md` enforces.

### [STD-CI-005] Feature flags
- **Applicability:** Partial
- **Statement:** Major features SHOULD be deployed behind a feature flag for gradual rollout.
- **Rationale:** Allows A/B testing, rollback without redeploy.
- **Verify:** No current implementation. Defer until traffic warrants.

### [STD-CI-006] Blue-green / canary deployment
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Production deploys MUST support zero-downtime rollback.
- **Rationale:** Vercel handles blue-green automatically. Manual promotion through env vars if needed.
- **Verify:** Vercel deployment history shows instant rollback capability.

### [STD-CI-007] Infrastructure as Code (IaC)
- **Applicability:** Partial
- **Statement:** Infrastructure SHOULD be defined in code (Terraform / Vercel CLI / Supabase migrations).
- **Rationale:** Reproducibility, audit trail.
- **Verify:** Supabase migrations ARE IaC. Vercel config is mostly via `vercel.json` / `next.config.ts`.

### [STD-TEST-001] Test-Driven Development (TDD)
- **Applicability:** Partial
- **Statement:** New server-side logic SHOULD be written test-first.
- **Rationale:** Vitest is configured. TDD discipline is encouraged but not enforced.
- **Verify:** Tests exist for new API routes, validators, balance config logic.

### [STD-TEST-002] Unit testing
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Pure functions, validators, and calculators MUST have unit tests.
- **Rationale:** 65 unit tests currently pass (validators, JWT, game tick, balance config, tier centralization).
- **Verify:** `tests/unit/*.test.ts` exists and passes.

### [STD-TEST-003] Integration testing
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** API endpoints MUST have integration tests covering auth + happy path + reject paths.
- **Rationale:** 32 API tests cover trade, action, state, definitions, market-history.
- **Verify:** `tests/api/game/*.test.ts` exists and passes.

### [STD-TEST-004] E2E testing (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Critical user flows SHOULD have end-to-end tests.
- **Rationale:** Playwright not yet configured. Smoke tests via manual checklist exist.
- **Verify:** N/A — defer until product/market fit.

### [STD-TEST-005] Performance testing
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Production SHOULD be load-tested for target user count.
- **Rationale:** No target SLA yet.
- **Verify:** N/A — defer until launch.

### [STD-TEST-006] Smoke testing on deploy
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Every production deploy MUST be smoke-tested manually before promotion. See [PRF-007].
- **Rationale:** Catches SSR errors, hydration mismatches, missing migrations.

### Frontend Performance

### [STD-PERF-001] SSR + ISR for fast first paint
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Pages MUST use Next.js SSR (App Router default) and ISR where possible.
- **Rationale:** Game has SSR for `/`, `/game/[tab]`, `/admin/`.
- **Verify:** `next.config.ts` confirms. Lighthouse score.

### [STD-PERF-002] Caching via CDN
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Static assets MUST be served from CDN (Vercel Edge Network).
- **Rationale:** Default Vercel behavior.
- **Verify:** Browser Network tab shows cache hit on static assets.

### [STD-PERF-003] Core Web Vitals
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Game pages MUST meet Core Web Vitals: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1.
- **Rationale:** User-perceived performance.
- **Verify:** Run Lighthouse in production. Track in Vercel Analytics.

### [STD-PERF-004] Server-side config caching
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Game config MUST be cached server-side (60s poller + `instrumentation.ts` pre-warm).
- **Rationale:** See [PER-005], [ARC-003]. Config rarely changes.

### Architecture Patterns

### [STD-ARC-001] Event-driven architecture (within server)
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Player actions trigger events (pressure updates, market ticks, contract fulfillment).
- **Rationale:** Server emits state changes via Supabase RPC + Realtime channel.
- **Verify:** `apply_market_tick` RPC, `upsert_market_pressure` RPC, presence channel.

### [STD-ARC-002] Idempotency for mutations
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Trade endpoints MUST be idempotent for the same `(user, idempotency_key)` within cooldown window.
- **Rationale:** Cooldown serves as natural idempotency window. Player can retry safely.
- **Verify:** Trade route returns `TRADE_COOLDOWN` 429 on retry. Trade state version conflict returns 409.

### [STD-ARC-003] Queues for async work (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Long-running async work (news generation, daily rewards) MAY move to a queue.
- **Rationale:** Currently `apply_market_tick` is sync. Cloudflare Worker for news is async via fetch.
- **Verify:** N/A — defer until work exceeds synchronous response budget.

### [STD-ARC-004] Pagination for list endpoints
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** List endpoints MUST paginate with LIMIT (default 50, max 200). See [PER-002].
- **Rationale:** Standard practice for unbounded data.

### [STD-ARC-005] Backup & recovery
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Supabase manages daily backups. Restore procedure documented.
- **Rationale:** Supabase Pro includes point-in-time recovery.
- **Verify:** Supabase project settings → Backups → confirm daily snapshots exist.

### [STD-ARC-006] Disaster recovery (DR)
- **Applicability:** Partial
- **Statement:** DR plan documented and tested annually.
- **Rationale:** No formal DR drill yet. Vercel + Supabase multi-region not configured.
- **Verify:** N/A — formal DR not yet required at current scale.

### [STD-I18N-001] Internationalization (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** All user-facing strings SHOULD be extracted to a translation key.
- **Rationale:** Currently English-only. i18n library (next-intl) not installed.
- **Verify:** N/A — defer until target market requires it.

### [STD-I18N-002] Localization for currencies / formats
- **Applicability:** Apply
- **Statement:** Number formatting MUST respect user locale (commas vs periods).
- **Rationale:** `formatNumber` utility handles locale-aware formatting.
- **Verify:** `src/lib/game/utils/formatNumber.ts`.

### [STD-SEO-001] SEO (future)
- **Applicability:** Future
- **Statement:** Marketing pages SHOULD have proper SEO meta tags.
- **Rationale:** Game is behind login (no public marketing pages yet).
- **Verify:** N/A — defer until marketing site exists.

### [STD-MONOREPO-001] Monorepo (future)
- **Applicability:** N/A
- **Statement:** Currently single Next.js app. If a second service emerges (e.g., dedicated game server), consider monorepo.
- **Rationale:** Single package, no inter-project shared code currently.

---

## Standards Summary

| Tier | Count | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| **Apply** | 22 | Enforced now (rules in this doc + tests) |
| **Partial** | 6 | Some implementation, gap documented |
| **Future** | 14 | Relevant post-launch (i18n, MFA, E2E, etc.) |
| **N/A** | 2 | Monorepo, SLA/SLO/SLI (no enterprise customers) |

**Critical-path gaps:**
1. **[STD-OBS-002]** Metrics — defer until traffic warrants, but plan now
2. **[STD-TEST-004]** E2E tests — defer until product/market fit, but track as known gap
3. **[STD-I18N-001]** Internationalization — defer until target market expands

